    },
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A gentle answer turns away anger,",
          "but a harsh word stirs up wrath."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The tongue of the wise makes knowledge attractive,",
          "but the mouth of fools blurts out foolishness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The eyes of the Lord are everywhere,",
          "observing the wicked and the good."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The tongue that heals is a tree of life,",
          "but a devious tongue breaks the spirit."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A fool despises his father’s discipline,",
          "but a person who accepts correction is sensible."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The house of the righteous has great wealth,",
          "but trouble accompanies the income of the wicked."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The lips of the wise broadcast knowledge,",
          "but not so the heart of fools."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The sacrifice of the wicked is detestable to the Lord,",
          "but the prayer of the upright is his delight."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord detests the way of the wicked,",
          "but he loves the one who pursues righteousness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Discipline is harsh for the one who leaves the path;",
          "the one who hates correction will die."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Sheol and Abaddon lie open before the Lord —",
          "how much more, human hearts."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A mocker doesn’t love one who corrects him;",
          "he will not consult the wise."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A joyful heart makes a face cheerful,",
          "but a sad heart produces a broken spirit."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A discerning mind seeks knowledge,",
          "but the mouth of fools feeds on foolishness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "All the days of the oppressed are miserable,",
          "but a cheerful heart has a continual feast."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Better a little with the fear of the Lord",
          "than great treasure with turmoil."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Better a meal of vegetables where there is love",
          "than a fattened ox with hatred."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A hot-tempered person stirs up conflict,",
          "but one slow to anger calms strife."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A slacker’s way is like a thorny hedge,",
          "but the path of the upright is a highway."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A wise son brings joy to his father,",
          "but a foolish man despises his mother."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Foolishness brings joy to one without sense,",
          "but a person with understanding walks a straight path."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Plans fail when there is no counsel,",
          "but with many advisers they succeed."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A person takes joy in giving an answer;",
          "and a timely word #— #how good that is!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the prudent the path of life leads upward,",
          "so that he may avoid going down to Sheol."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord tears apart the house of the proud,",
          "but he protects the widow’s territory."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord detests the plans of the one who is evil,",
          "but pleasant words are pure."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The one who profits dishonestly troubles his household,",
          "but the one who hates bribes will live."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The mind of the righteous person thinks before answering,",
          "but the mouth of the wicked blurts out evil things."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord is far from the wicked,",
          "but he hears the prayer of the righteous."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Bright eyes cheer the heart;",
          "good news strengthens the bones."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "One who listens to life-giving rebukes",
          "will be at home among the wise."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Anyone who ignores discipline despises himself,",
          "but whoever listens to correction acquires good sense. ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The fear of the Lord is what wisdom teaches,",
          "and humility comes before honor."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
